From: Alvaro Moran <alvaro.moran@huggingface.co>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:19:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(model): replicate KV heads when TP exceeds them

With fewer KV heads than tensor-parallel ranks, as vLLM does on GPU,
replicate the KV heads instead of failing: each rank keeps the k/v
projection rows of the one KV head its query heads attend with. The TP
size and the number of KV heads must divide one another.

Add a CPU test that shards a tiny random Llama over simulated ranks
(threads, in-process all-reduce) and checks the logits against the
unsharded model, for plain and replicated KV heads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
